## Context
Filed from the JETP Observer night raid e34cf5 (2026-11-08, padme). On padme a
clean JETP origin/main fails exactly two `make check-fast` nodes
(tests/test_jetp_text_adapters.py, stdlib html.parser difference, JETP ticket
2098). verify-gate bounces any red declared check; `root_cause_class: Original
Error` labels it but still REROLLs, and round 2 ESCALATEs. JETP PR #261 (a
two-line test-fixture fix, all exit criteria ADDRESSED) went REROLL then
ESCALATE on that baseline alone; every other PR of the raid hits the same wall,
so nothing can merge from padme until 2098 is fixed.

## Ask
Decide whether verify-gate admits a mechanically proven baseline: the branch's
failing node set equals a fresh run on clean origin/main on the same host and
venv, the diff touches no file of those nodes, the record quotes both lists and
a ticket. Or state that a host with a red baseline cannot gate, so callers know
to fix the baseline first.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] verify-gate states its rule for a pre-existing red declared check, with a test
